  "id": "Compound::DB00777 - Gene::1812",
  "verbalization": "Propiomazine is implicated in the interaction with G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptors through its binding to Chrm1, Chrm2, and Chrm5, all of which participate in G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity. This pathway leads to a direct involvement of Drd1, a receptor that is part of the G-protein coupled activity. The evidence suggests that Propiomazine may act through a common mechanism involving the activation of G-protein coupled receptors, which in turn influence Drd1. The overlapping roles of these receptors in the G-protein pathway provide a unified explanation for the observed relationship between Propiomazine and Drd1. The integration of these paths highlights a potential mechanism where Propiomazine modulates receptor activity, leading to a downstream effect on Drd1. The evidence supports a role for Propiomazine in the regulation of G-protein coupled receptor function, which is a key pathway in neurotransmission and may underlie its interaction with Drd1.",
